description be updated accordingly?"]],0,41],[7095650,20411,234,4.21,3.407,[[3,26]],[["09f14383_2f22d0dc",58,-2,1,"nit: the line break seems incorrect"],["0b43d762_39a5f9bb",3,-2,0,"thank you for the screenshots!"],["147c70c7_c6f2741c",79,-2,1,"nit: the previous version actually provides better readability, would you mind keeping it? (also we can rename the `visibility` variable to `secondaryButtonVisibility` instead)"],["31805ec5_576e16f1",59,-2,1,"Same for the `layout_marginHorizontal` (and the preference for Start/End otherwise)"],["32e1b385_c3896dca",79,-2,0,"The `if` switch is quite long and difficult to read already unfortunately. would you mind extract the logic into a private method? (e.g. somthing like `showSigninLayout(boolean showLayout)`)"],["3e647b5f_cebed648",62,-2,1,"nit: Do we need to put the `signed_out` suffix as we don't have a value for signed-in promo?"],["4b0725ae_cbca75a8",79,-2,0,"Can we remove this block? we don't use the value of `shouldShowSignedInLayout` here, so the same margins will be applied to the layout regardless of the signed-in state. (I suppose we don't want a…"],["4de4936a_ba118bed",59,-2,1,"ditto for the horizontal margins"],["5bcc5a52_462182a4",79,-2,1,"this seems repeated for the case where we have `!shouldShowSignedInLayout` below. Can we remove those 2 blocks?"],["7352dfdc_c1da8d97",58,-2,1,"nit: (here and above) I was a bit confused by the experiment wording, the reader might miss the context for `two buttons` layout and not understand the details of why the field is not supposed to be…"],["7694a9a5_750d5b2b",79,-2,1,"nit: it's better to extract to a separate variable for readability, same for the calls below."],["957c57c8_e49ae3ff",59,-2,1,"nit: you can add `horizontal` in the dimen naming to clarify its usage and keep consistency with other dimens (yes it would make it longer though ^^')"],["ac6417f3_d501096b",63,-2,1,"nit: we can match the string to the variable name for consistency ```suggestion new PropertyModel.WritableBooleanPropertyKey(\"should_show_signed_in_layout\"); ```"],["b706fbbe_740a3e2b",59,-2,1,"ditto for the horizontal margins"],["dd611ecf_aa785ae3",62,-2,0,"nit: you can use `layout_marginHorizontal` Note that we usually recommend using Start/End instead of Left/Right for padding setting to be able to better adapt to right-to-left languages layout. (Here…"],["f071055b_87226387",82,-2,0,"Thank you for extracting the dimens!"],["fb1db18d_c968a285",79,-2,1,"ditto, this is called in the block above"],["8285c845_57b5e716",79,0,1,"nit: maybe `SignedIn` would be more accurate?"]],0,42],[7156131,20412,110,2.361,1.866,[[3,27]],[["6a0a3b81_6c33447b",81,-3,1,"Can we move this to the `setUp` method instead? Using `mockingDetails(delegate).isMock()` seems to be an antipattern from my perspective."],["c6e8746d_95e70041",81,-3,1,"Nit: consider removing this overload and explicitly passing the delegate where `createSigninPromoMediator` is invoked."]],0,43],[7171208,20413,16,0.737,0.556,[[3,28]],[["9e93fb4f_f39249a5",76,-1,1,"nit: Please add argument prefixes for these properties except for profileData. Example: ``` /* titleString= */ \"\", ```"]],0,44],[7171209,20423,174,4.21,3.407,[[3,29]],[["0d0700d9_05d46859",3,-11,0,"thank you for the recording!"],["4bd169fb_c1075de1",79,-11,1,"I think we shouldn't put this line here: if profile data is set, we could be in the signed-in state as well and this logic could interfere with the other properties and could be error-prone, e.g. in…"],["9bbc6254_06352009",76,-11,1,"(see comment below) if this will control only the header, should we rename it to something like `SHOULD_SHOW_HEADER_WITH_AVATAR`? it will allow us to further decouple the view property from the…"],["c906b782_9d83dc57",76,-11,1,"would you mind adding a test for the flow which triggers this bug? so we'll cover this case in the future even if the logic changes"],["ca7b1c34_b33a7d36",76,-11,1,"(Related to the comment below) should we also hide it when we should show the signed-